Boundary divisors -- irreducible components of the boundary of the moduli space of stable n-pointed genus zero curves
*********************************************************************************************************************

Let $\Delta_I$ be the closure of the locus of curves with two irreducible
components meeting at one node such that the marked points with labels in $I$
lie on the first component, and the marked points with labels in $I^c$ lie on
the second component.  Then $\Delta_I$ is an irreducible effective divisor.

Let $\delta_I$ be the class of $\Delta_I$.  Then the classes $\{ \delta_I : \#I
\geq 2, \#I \leq n/2, 1 \in I if \#I=n/2\}$ span the Picard group of
$\bar{M}_{0,n}$.  The relations between these classes are called the Keel
relations.

